# --- Environment files — NEVER commit credentials -------------------------
# `.env` and every variant (`.env.local`, `.env.production`, `.env.example`,
# `.env.*.local`, `*.env`) is git-ignored in every directory, including
# templates: a template that ships real keys is a leak. Committing one keeps
# it in the repo history forever, so treat any committed env file as public.
.env
.env.*
.env*.local
*.env
.expo/
.expo-shared/
*.log
.DS_Store
.next/
out/
coverage/
.mongo/
*.tsbuildinfo